        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John J. Pershing\n- Events: Battle of Saint-Mihiel\n- Organizations: American Expeditionary Force, United States Army\n- Places: Western Front\n- Topics: World War I\n\nFacts:\n- John J. Pershing was born on September 13, 1860, and died on July 15, 1948.\n- John J. Pershing was a senior United States Army officer and held the rank of General of the Armies.\n- John J. Pershing served as commander of the American Expeditionary Force on the Western Front during World War I from 1917 to 1918.\n- The Battle of Saint-Mihiel was fought from September 12 to September 15, 1918, during World War I.\n- The Battle of Saint-Mihiel involved the American Expeditionary Force and 110,000 French troops under the command of John J. Pershing against German positions.",
